# Text selection and the clipboard: a run selected by name, a drag across
# words, Shift with the arrow keys, select-all, copy, and paste into a
# field. The clipboard is the process's own during a script, so nothing the
# user copied is touched. The content area starts 76 px down (tab strip +
# toolbar), the first paragraph sits 24 px below that (the body margin and
# its own top margin), and its text starts 8 px in; Sashfold Mono at 16px is
# 10 px per glyph, so the drag coordinates below land on known glyphs.
resize 800 500
open data:text/html,<title>Selection</title><style>body{margin:8px;font-family:"Sashfold Mono";font-size:16px;line-height:20px}</style><p>The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.</p><p>Second line of text here.</p><form><input name="q"></form>
assert-title Selection
assert-selection

select-text quick brown
assert-selection quick brown
assert-golden goldens/selection-words.png
key ctrl+c
focus q
key ctrl+v
assert-value q quick brown
key Escape

drag 30 102 120 102
assert-selection e quick b

select-text The
key shift+right
key shift+right
assert-selection The q
key shift+end
assert-selection The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.
key shift+left
assert-selection The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog
key shift+down
assert-golden goldens/selection-lines.png
key Escape
assert-selection

key ctrl+a
assert-golden goldens/selection-all.png
key Escape
assert-selection
